<section class="brain-spine-section" style="background:#f8f9fa">
  <h2 class="brain-spine-title">Root Cause in Ayurveda</h2>
  <div class="brain-spine-divider"></div>
  <p>Classical Ayurveda describes reproductive health as being governed by Shukra dhatu, the seventh and final tissue in the Dhatu formation sequence. This means Shukra quality depends on the health of every preceding tissue: Rasa (plasma), Rakta (blood), Mamsa (muscle), Meda (fat), Asthi (bone) and Majja (nervous tissue). Any disruption upstream affects Shukra quality downstream.</p>
  <p>Specific classical frameworks apply. Vandhyatva describes female infertility with sub-classifications. Klaibya describes erectile dysfunction with specific Vajikarana approaches. Shukra Dushti describes semen abnormalities with therapeutic protocols for correction.</p>
  <p>This foundational understanding shapes the Ayurveda treatment in Hyderabad approach at KSAC Hospitals. Rather than treating fertility or sexology concerns in isolation, our senior physicians assess the entire Dhatu chain, Agni function and dosha balance to plan individualised care.</p>
</section>

<section class="brain-spine-section">
  <h2 class="brain-spine-title">How Ayurveda Offers Fertility and Sexology Care</h2>
  <div class="brain-spine-divider"></div>
  <div class="if-tx-grid">
    <div class="if-tx-card"><h4>Shodhana (Pre-Fertility Cleansing)</h4><p>Classical Ayurveda emphasises <a href="/pages/panchakarma-therapies-detox" style="color:#3c8dbc">Panchakarma cleansing</a> before Vajikarana or Rasayana therapy. Virechana and Basti protocols to clear accumulated Ama and optimise Dhatu formation.</p></div>
    <div class="if-tx-card"><h4>Vajikarana (Reproductive Ayurveda)</h4><p>The entire branch of classical Ayurveda dedicated to reproductive wellness, sexual health and progeny support. Specific herbal formulations, dietary protocols and procedures selected by the treating physician.</p></div>
    <div class="if-tx-card"><h4>Rasayana (Rejuvenation)</h4><p>Rasayana to restore Dhatu strength and overall vitality. Reproductive Rasayana preparations prescribed individually based on assessment.</p></div>
    <div class="if-tx-card"><h4>Uttar Basti (Female Fertility)</h4><p>Classical uterine cleansing and nourishment procedure for suitable cases of female infertility. Requires careful patient selection and physician supervision.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="if-tx-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:400px">
    <div class="if-tx-card"><h4>Dietary and Lifestyle Modification</h4><p>Individualised dietary guidance, sleep optimisation, stress management, exercise structuring and reproductive tissue-specific nutrition planning for both partners.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:14px;color:#888;font-style:italic;text-align:center!important">All treatment plans are decided after consultation and assessment. Outcomes vary from person to person. KSAC does not guarantee pregnancy.</p>
</section>

