<section class="brain-spine-section">
  <h2 class="brain-spine-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="brain-spine-divider"></div>
  <div class="pt-faq" style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto">
    <details><summary>Can Ayurvedic treatment guarantee pregnancy?</summary><p class="faq-a">No. KSAC Hospitals does not guarantee pregnancy through Ayurvedic treatment. Fertility outcomes depend on many factors. Ayurvedic fertility care is designed to optimise the conditions for conception by improving reproductive tissue health, hormonal balance and overall wellness.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is Ayurvedic infertility treatment a replacement for IVF?</summary><p class="faq-a">No. Ayurvedic fertility care is not a replacement for IUI, IVF or ICSI where these are clinically indicated. Cases with significant tubal factor, severe male factor or conditions requiring assisted reproduction are supported alongside, not instead of, conventional reproductive medicine.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can Ayurveda increase sperm count for azoospermia?</summary><p class="faq-a">Azoospermia has many possible causes including obstructive, non-obstructive, hormonal, genetic and post-infectious factors. An andrologist evaluation is required before any Ayurvedic supportive care is considered. Not all forms of azoospermia are amenable to Ayurvedic intervention.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is the consultation confidential?</summary><p class="faq-a">Yes. All fertility and sexology consultations at KSAC Hospitals are completely confidential. Patient information is protected under NABH accreditation standards. Same-gender clinical staff are available on request.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does KSAC accept insurance for fertility treatment?</summary><p class="faq-a">Insurance coverage for fertility treatment varies by insurer and policy. KSAC Hospitals is NABH accredited and empanelled with the State Government of Telangana. We support insurance direct billing where applicable, CGHS, ECHS and dedicated international patient services.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

